    <text x="522" y="196" class="note">what it reports</text>
    <text x="510.0" y="324.0" class="note" text-anchor="end">flagged-only: 0</text>
  </svg>
  {caption && <figcaption>The same 30 labels per batch, spent three ways, averaged over runs (3-batch rolling mean). Labelling only the tweets you dispatched on reports zero misses forever, because a miss is by definition a tweet you didn&#x27;t flag. Labelling near the threshold sees only the misses that were nearly caught. Diverting a fifth of the budget to a random audit, weighted back up, tracks the real count: about 17 a batch once the storm hits.</figcaption>}
</figure>

<style>
  .fig { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin: 1.6rem auto 0.6rem; }
  .fig text { font-family: var(--font-jetbrains); fill: var(--text-dim); }
  .fig .tick { font-size: 12px; }
  .fig .label { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .fig .mid { text-anchor: middle; }
  .fig .end { text-anchor: end; }
  .fig .grid { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .fig .axis { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1.5; }
  .fig .ref { stroke: var(--text-muted); stroke-width: 1.5; stroke-dasharray: 4 4; fill: none; }
  .fig .series { fill: none; stroke-width: 2; stroke-linecap: round; stroke-linejoin: round; }
  .fig .key { font-size: 12.5px; fill: var(--text); }
  .fig .note { font-size: 11.5px; fill: var(--text-muted); }
  .fig .big { font-size: 13px; fill: var(--text); }
  figcaption {
    font-family: var(--font-jetbrains);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: 0 auto 2.2rem;
    text-align: center;
  }
</style>
